  "explanation": {
    "md_es": "**Preguntar:** *What do you do? · What's your job? · Where do you work?* (¿dónde trabajas?)\n\n**Responder:**\n\n- **I'm** + profesión (con *a/an*): *I'm an engineer. · She's a lawyer.*\n- **I work as** + profesión: *I work as a chef.* (trabajo de…)\n- **I work in** + lugar o sector: *I work in an office / in a factory / in education.*\n- **I work for** + empresa o jefe: *I work for a big company.*\n- **I work at** + lugar concreto: *I work at a hospital / at Tesco.*\n\n**Estudios:** *I'm a student. · I study law at university. · I'm in my second year.*\n\n**job / work:** *job* es contable (*a job, two jobs*); **work** es incontable (*I have a lot of work.*, no *works*). *Full-time* (tiempo completo) y *part-time* (medio tiempo).\n\n**Ojo, falsos amigos:** *career* es la trayectoria profesional (la 'carrera universitaria' es *degree*); *college* no es 'colegio' (colegio = *school*).\n\nPronunciación: *engineer* /ˌendʒɪˈnɪə/ (acento al final) · *colleague* /ˈkɒliːɡ/ · *receptionist* /rɪˈsepʃənɪst/.",
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "I am work in a bank.",
        "right": "I work in a bank.",
        "note": "No se combina am con work."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "I have a lot of works.",
        "right": "I have a lot of work.",
        "note": "Work es incontable."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": [
      {
        "word": "career",
        "es_false": "carrera (universitaria)",
        "real": "trayectoria profesional",
        "note": "La carrera universitaria se dice degree o university course."
      }
    ]
  },
